# Docker build-context exclusions for the SelahCue Platform API image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# .gitignore does NOT filter a Docker build context. A clean `git status` says
# nothing about what `docker build` uploads, and the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`
# from this directory (compose: `build: ./api`). Without these rules every image
# permanently bakes:
#
#   * api/.env      -> SECRET_KEY, the HMAC pepper behind every device-token,
#                      credential-token and email fingerprint in the system,
#                      plus SQL_PASSWORD. The documented dev workflow REQUIRES
#                      this file to exist here (env_file: ./api/.env).
#   * db.sqlite3    -> real dev data: password hashes, token fingerprints.
#   * caches        -> .pytest_cache/, __pycache__/, *.egg-info/ (host-built).
#
# The compose bind-mount (./api:/usr/src/app) only *masks* those paths at run
# time; it does not remove them from the image. `docker save`, a registry push,
# or `docker history` still hands the pepper to whoever has the image.
#
# PATTERN SEMANTICS TRAP
# ----------------------
# Unlike .gitignore, .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the context root:
# a bare `__pycache__/` matches ONLY the top-level one. Use `**/` for anything
# that can nest. Exceptions (`!`) must come after the pattern they undo — the
# last matching pattern wins.
#
# Keep this list in step with api/.gitignore.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# ...except the committed sample, which carries key NAMES and dev placeholders
# only (same exception api/.gitignore makes). Kept in the image so anyone who
# shells into a container can see which keys the app expects. Must stay below
# the two patterns above.
!.env.sample

# --- Local dev databases -----------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal

# --- Build / test artefacts (all regenerated inside the image) ---------------
# *.egg-info in particular: a host-built editable-install stub copied into the
# image would shadow the one the Dockerfile builds for the container.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Virtualenvs (host-built: wrong platform, and large) ---------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- VCS, editor and OS noise ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# NOT excluded on purpose: tests/ and pytest.ini (the image installs the [dev]
# extra so `pytest` can run inside the container) and README.md.
